In a Blazor Web App, this page has **no** `@rendermode`. You open `/a` and click the button 3 times.

```razor
@page "/a"

<p>Count: @count</p>
<button @onclick="() => count++">+1</button>

@code {
    private int count;
}
```

**What does the page show after 3 clicks?**

Same page, one line added. You click the button 3 times.

```razor
@page "/b"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<p>Count: @count</p>
<button @onclick="() => count++">+1</button>

@code {
    private int count;
}
```

**What does the page show, and what travels over the network on each click?**

```razor
@page "/c"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<p>Hello</p>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("C initialized");
    }
}
```

**You load `/c` once (a full page load). How many times does "C initialized" print, and where?**
